hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"389","On the authority of Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa’sa’a, on the authority of his father, who said: Saeed: If you are in the desert, raise your voice in the call, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No tree can hear his voice. “And there is no earth, nor stone, nor jinn, nor man, but it bears witness to it.” He once said: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’saa told me. My father told me. He was an orphan in Abu Sa’id’s care, and his mother was With Abu Saeed"
"390","On the authority of Bandar Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, who said: I heard Abu Yahya, saying: I heard Abu Kitten, says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The muezzin will be forgiven for the extent of his voice, and everything wet and dry will bear witness to him, and every witness will bear witness to him.” Prayer and twenty-five good deeds are recorded for him, and what comes between them is expiated for him.” Abu Bakr said: He means what is between the two prayers."
